## Summary

The change: Auto-watch now defaults to lint+test instead of test-only, closing the biggest competitive gap with Aider (which auto-lints every file it edits).

**What changed in src/commands_dev.rs**:
1. `auto_detect_watch_command()` — now calls detect_watch_all_command() instead of `detect_test_command(). For Rust projects, this means auto-watch runs cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings && cargo test` instead of just cargo test.
2. Bare `/watch` — the "" match arm now also uses detect_watch_all_command(), so typing /watch with no arguments gets lint+test just like /watch all.
3. `/watch lint` — new subcommand that sets watch to the lint-only command (e.g. cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings), for when you want fast lint feedback without running the full test suite.
4. `WATCH_SUBCOMMANDS` — added "lint" for tab completion.
5. `detect_test_command()` — made private with #[allow(dead_code)] since nothing calls it anymore (superseded by detect_watch_all_command which already falls back to test-only when no lint is available).

What changed in `src/help.rs`:
• Updated all `/watch help strings to reflect lint+test as the default, mention the new /watch lint` option.

New tests (3):
• watch_subcommands_includes_lint — verifies "lint" is in the tab-completion list
• `handle_watch_lint_sets_lint_only_command — verifies /watch lint` sets clippy-only (no test)
• handle_watch_bare_sets_lint_and_test — verifies bare /watch now sets lint && test

The infrastructure was already there — `detect_watch_all_command(), lint_command_for_project()`, the whole watch-after-prompt loop. This was truly just connecting the right pipe. 🐙

